{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The SanDisk card feels useful as a spare for trying Raspberry Pi installations, provided it is compatible with my setup.",
    "The wired Panasonic earbuds connect with my interest in laptop audio, although that connection alone does not give me a reason to replace headphones I already have."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "The streaming sticks do not follow from my HDMI cable and Raspberry Pi purchases: those support setting up equipment, while I have no current need for a streaming player.",
    "The tablets, Echo Dot, and smart plug would introduce devices without solving a need I have expressed. Having a Kindle does not mean I want more screens or an Alexa setup.",
    "The portable speaker misses why headphones fit my setup: I use personal computer audio and have no current need for room or outdoor playback."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My electronics purchases seem to have been treated as broad interest in any electronic gadget, rather than interest in accessories with a specific practical use.",
    "My Kindle purchase seems to have been stretched into interest in other Amazon devices, even though reading does not imply a need for streaming or home automation."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My latest interactions emphasize wired connectivity, computer cleaning, carrying equipment, and organizing my desk; useful additions should connect to those tasks.",
    "My Raspberry Pi, case, and memory-card history makes compatible storage useful for experimentation, whereas another standalone entertainment device has no clear role.",
    "Existing ownership matters: an extra memory card can support another installation, while another pair of headphones needs a clearer benefit before I would choose it."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations recognized my interest in electronics but mostly missed my current focus on practical additions to my computer, networking, and Raspberry Pi setup."
}"}
